# Take-off thrust gap decomposition (P5.2 Step 2)

Calibration `outputs/calibration_trent1000_ae3_v4.json`; turbine analytic, nozzle analytic, xi from record, Jet-A1, v4 phi_to/eta_b/p_loss. Target 310.9 kN (data/icao_engine_data.csv 'Rated Thrust (kN)', UID 02P23RR126, Power 100 %). Generated by `scripts/validation/takeoff_thrust_gap.py`. **Every counterfactual below is a diagnostic, not a fix; no input value is adopted.**

## 1. Where the thrust comes from

| Term | kN |
|---|---|
| Core nozzle, momentum m(u_e − u_in) | 55.3914545 |
| Core nozzle, pressure (p_e − p_amb)A_e | 0.0000000 |
| Bypass m_bp·u_bp (u_bp = 256.11 m/s) | 186.2185401 |
| **Model total** | **241.6099946** |
| Target (ICAO rated) | 310.9 |
| **Gap** | **69.2900 (22.3 %)** |

Core stream 82.2182069 kg/s (air + fuel), bypass 727.09 kg/s; T4 1894.9 K; fan work 26.20 MW.

## 2. Thrust-equation audit

The engine-level static thrust is F = m_e·u_e − m_0·u_0 + (p_e − p_0)A_e with u_0 = 0 ([NASA general thrust equation](https://www1.grc.nasa.gov/beginners-guide-to-aeronautics/thrust-force/) subtracts *freestream* inlet momentum). The analytic core nozzle subtracts the momentum at its own inlet, the turbine exit: 82.2182069 kg/s × 200.6901102 m/s = **16.5003810 kN**. That velocity is itself set by continuity through `A_combustor_exit × 1.82`, an area choice.

- Restoring that term alone: **258.1103756 kN**, still **52.7896244 kN** (17.0 %) below target.

## 3. Nozzle pressure / area / choking

| Stream | p0/p_amb | critical | choked (convergent)? |
|---|---|---|---|
| Core | 3.644 | 1.820 | yes |
| Bypass | 1.450 | 1.893 | no |

The analytic nozzle always expands to p_amb (the pressure term is zero by construction) and never uses its design exit area (0.340 m²); full expansion needs 0.2374 m². A convergent core nozzle from the same stagnation state (throat 0.1955 m²) gives 70.6038 kN gross vs 71.8918 kN fully expanded — lower, so nozzle treatment does not explain the shortfall. The bypass stream is unchoked; its full expansion is exact for a convergent nozzle.

