## Verdict: **STRUCTURAL**

The production thrust equation contains an incorrect term (nozzle-inlet momentum subtracted at an internal station), worth 16.5004 kN; per docs/plan.md P5.2 Step 2 this is a missing/incorrect model term, not a mis-set input, so fitting thrust now would hide it in a parameter. Restoring it alone leaves 52.7896 kN (17.0 %) unexplained; no single input in the tested ranges is sourced, so none is adopted.

Per docs/plan.md P5.2 Step 2 this is an escalation gate: P5.2 Steps 3–4 (v5 objective and fit) and everything downstream stop until the user decides the repair.

